ing not because i'm studying tables  that's my view  so  if we say that our goal is to  communicate to get enough input  and and certainly all the reading that  i've done on how the brain works would  certainly support the view that the  brain will eventually figure things out  the main thing is not to discourage the  learner and it's precisely because of  the kind of  language teaching methods that liam  proposes that most people do poorly at  school the swedes speak english because  they have so much english around them on  television and elsewhere but it's not  because of what they learn in school  the schools with their emphasis on  language on on on grammar instruction  and memorizing tables they just  frustrate everybody because it's not a  very efficient way to learn for most  people but i don't deny liam that is  probably for you if you like doing it  that way i'm sure it is good for you but  you are in the minority in my experience  the vast majority of people are far  better off to be exposed to a lot of  enjoyable input  at their level that they have selected  struggle a bit  uh with the meaning of some of the words  things are a little bit fuzzy they say  words and phrases they keep doing it  they listen they read they listen many  times and slowly the language comes into  focus  and that is more enjoyable  and a more natural way to learn and that  is not limited to people under five  because i've done it many many times  and  it's interesting the the dogmatic now  some people might say that i'm dogmatic  perhaps i am but i don't deny the  possibility that there are people like  liam but i in my experience i consider  them to be very much the minority and if  i look at  research on how the brain learns things  where it's clear that the brain is  even from an evolutionary perspective is  not at go as good in dealing with  logical explanations  and and and rules presented to it  as it is in naturally identifying  patterns and creating its own rules and  cr